Subject: [PATCH] audio_a2dp_hw: let the system image have audio.a2dp.default

audio.a2dp.default is the "a2dp" module of an audio policy: the audio HAL loads it
and hands it the Bluetooth stream, which it passes to the stack over the sockets in
/data/misc/bluedroid. Android 13 still has that path, for an audio HAL that knows no
Bluetooth Audio HAL; the ASUS ZenPad 3S 10 (MSM8956) has one such HAL. But the
module is available only to the Bluetooth APEX, and a product that installs it in
the system image fails the platform availability check.

Its one obstacle was libosi, which is APEX-only together with most of the stack it
links. The module used four functions from it. It now compiles the three libosi
sources that hold them (hash_map_utils, properties, socket_local_client), through a
filegroup, and, instead of libosi's allocator, which goes through the allocation
tracker and with it the stack's logging, three libc-backed functions of its own: in
the audio HAL the tracker is never switched on, so they are the same. With no libosi
it can be "//apex_available:platform" as well.
---
diff --git a/system/audio_a2dp_hw/Android.bp b/system/audio_a2dp_hw/Android.bp
index 408c49f..6c2eb97 100644
--- a/system/audio_a2dp_hw/Android.bp
+++ b/system/audio_a2dp_hw/Android.bp
@@ -27,15 +27,17 @@ cc_library {
     srcs: [
         "src/audio_a2dp_hw.cc",
         "src/audio_a2dp_hw_utils.cc",
+        "src/osi_allocator.cc",
+        ":OsiAudioA2dpHwSources",
     ],
     apex_available: [
+        "//apex_available:platform",
         "com.android.bluetooth",
     ],
     shared_libs: [
         "liblog",
         "libcutils",
     ],
-    static_libs: ["libosi"],
 }
 
 cc_library_static {
diff --git a/system/audio_a2dp_hw/src/osi_allocator.cc b/system/audio_a2dp_hw/src/osi_allocator.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5459146
--- /dev/null
+++ b/system/audio_a2dp_hw/src/osi_allocator.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+/*
+ * The three allocation functions of libosi that hash_map_utils.cc, compiled into
+ * audio.a2dp.default from libosi's sources, calls. libosi's allocator.cc passes them
+ * through its allocation tracker, which is switched on only in the Bluetooth
+ * process and brings the stack's logging with it; in the audio HAL it is never on,
+ * and then they are libc's.
+ */
+
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "osi/include/allocator.h"
+
+char* osi_strdup(const char* str) {
+  char* copy = strdup(str);
+  if (copy == NULL) abort();
+  return copy;
+}
+
+char* osi_strndup(const char* str, size_t len) {
+  char* copy = strndup(str, len);
+  if (copy == NULL) abort();
+  return copy;
+}
+
+void osi_free(void* ptr) { free(ptr); }
diff --git a/system/osi/Android.bp b/system/osi/Android.bp
index bcbac81..d63d138 100644
--- a/system/osi/Android.bp
+++ b/system/osi/Android.bp
@@ -52,6 +52,18 @@ filegroup {
   ],
 }
 
+// The parts of libosi that audio.a2dp.default uses. It is installed in the system
+// image for devices whose audio HAL still loads it, and libosi, with all it links,
+// is only available to the Bluetooth APEX.
+filegroup {
+  name: "OsiAudioA2dpHwSources",
+  srcs: [
+    "src/hash_map_utils.cc",
+    "src/properties.cc",
+    "src/socket_utils/socket_local_client.cc",
+  ],
+}
+
 // libosi static library for target
 cc_library_static {
     name: "libosi",
